---
import { toolbox, stats } from '../data/site';
---
<section class="sec" id="about">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="head"><h2 data-reveal>About</h2></header>
    <div class="about">
      <div class="about__text" data-reveal>
        <p class="lede">I work where cloud infrastructure meets a real business problem, as a founding member of Indonesia's first EdgeOne solutions architect team at Tencent Cloud.</p>
        <p>The job is half engineering and half persuasion: designing CDN, WAF and Anti-DDoS architectures that hold under a national bank's traffic, then explaining the trade-offs to executives who care about outcomes, not packets. Before Tencent I shipped ML models and ETL pipelines for financial institutions and retailers across Indonesia.</p>
        <p>I'm now reading an MSc in Smart Industries and Digital Transformation at NUS, and looking for 2026/27 internships in cloud, platform or applied ML.</p>
        <ul class="chips">
          {['Request for Proposal (RFP)','Computer Vision','Predictive Analytics','Edge Computing','Cloud Security'].map(c => <li>{c}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <aside class="toolbox" data-reveal>
        <h3>What I work with</h3>
        <dl>{toolbox.map(([k, v]) => <div><dt>{k}</dt><dd>{v}</dd></div>)}</dl>
      </aside>
    </div>
    <div class="stats">
      {stats.map(s => <div class="stat" data-reveal><b><span data-count={s.n}>0</span>{s.suffix}</b><span>{s.label}</span></div>)}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
